<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Porta Rosa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">4th century BCE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Porta Rosa is a stone gateway of the 4th century BCE at the site of Elea, Roman Velia, in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/campania">Campania</a>, southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>. Spanning a road between the two quarters of the city, it uses a true round arch of fitted wedge-shaped stones, among the earliest known in Greek architecture. It was uncovered in 1964.</p></div>
